<H1>Medium data</H1>
Search for medium no. = [1111].
<HR>
Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121&#176;C for 15 min.
<HR>
<P><B><FONT SIZE=3>1111&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ANAEROBIC ALKALINE LB MEDIUM</FONT></B></P>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> LB broth powder </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;25.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Tris base </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;3.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Distilled water </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;800.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml   </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Mix components thoroughly, adjust pH to 9.5 with NaOH and autoclave under a N<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (4:1, v/v) gas mixture.  After cooling, add aseptically and anaerobically the following solutions (autoclaved and stored under N<sub>2</sub>):  <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 8% Na<sub>2</sub>CO<sub>3</sub> solution </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;200.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 5% Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O solution </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;8.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml        </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
